0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
45. 690.8899999999999864 Td
(An important paradigm of natural language processing consists of large-scale pre-training on general domain data and) Tj
T* (adaptation to particular tasks. As we pre-train larger models, full fine-tuning, which retrains all model parameters, becomes less) Tj
T* (feasible. We propose Low-Rank Adaptation, or LoRA, which freezes the pre-trained model weights and injects trainable rank) Tj
T* (decomposition matrices into each layer of the Transformer architecture, greatly reducing the number of trainable parameters for) Tj
T* (downstream tasks.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.263 0.22 0.792 rg
45. 612.8899999999999864 Td
(4 Method) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
10.3499999999999996 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
45. 596.8899999999999864 Td
(A neural network contains many dense layers which perform matrix multiplication. The weight matrices in these layers typically) Tj
T* (have full-rank. When adapting to a specific task, Aghajanyan et al. \(2020\) shows that the pre-trained language models have a) Tj
T* (low "intrinsic dimension". Inspired by this, we hypothesize the updates to the weights also have a low "intrinsic rank" during) Tj
T* (adaptation. For a pre-trained weight matrix W0 in R^\(d x k\), we constrain its update by representing the latter with a low-rank) Tj
T* (decomposition W0 + Delta W = W0 + BA, where B in R^\(d x r\), A in R^\(r x k\), and the rank r << min\(d, k\).) Tj
ET
